    "body": "## Summary\n\n- some uploaded videos fail to play in Chrome's native `<video>` decoder. divine-web already handles this with HLS.js fallback to transcoded segments — the admin UI didn't have it.\n- adds `HlsVideo` component: tries native MP4 first, falls back to HLS.js (`media.divine.video/{hash}/hls/master.m3u8`), then to the authenticated media proxy for gated content\n- distinguishes \"content not available\" (404/deleted) from \"failed to load\" (other errors) in the media preview UI\n- fixes the `showByDefault` race condition where media would flash-show then collapse as report priority data loaded (tri-state `hasHighPriorityReports`)\n- adds `Access-Control-Allow-Credentials: true` to worker CORS headers (required for the credentialed media proxy fetch). `credentials: include` is scoped to the two media-proxy fetches only — no other API calls are affected\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] open a report with video content at relay.admin.divine.video — videos that previously showed as black rectangles with inactive controls should now play via HLS\n- [ ] open a report with image content — images still load normally\n- [ ] open a report with a high-priority category — media should start hidden\n- [ ] open a report with a non-high-priority category — media should start visible\n- [ ] verify no CORS errors in browser console on report list or report detail pages\n- [ ] verify deleted/unavailable media shows \"Content not available\" (ImageOff icon) instead of generic warning triangle",
